{"id": "EUVD-2026-105098", "enisaUuid": "8e119b09-401d-35e7-85a5-5d16f8744e22", "description": "Networknt light-4j from 2.1.5 before 2.4.0 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability in BasicAuthHandler that allows unauthenticated attackers to log in as LDAP/AD-delegated users. Attackers can send a Basic Authorization header with a known username and empty password, triggering an unauthenticated LDAP bind that is accepted as successful authentication.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T15:40:42", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/networknt/light-4j/issues/2804", "https://github.com/networknt/light-4j/pull/2805", "https://github.com/networknt/light-4j/commit/54743badb34260b76ed131d8b6a4f60210cc3673", "https://github.com/networknt/light-4j/releases/tag/2.4.0", "https://github.com/networknt/light-4j/blob/2.3.7/basic-auth/src/main/java/com/networknt/basicauth/BasicAuthHandler.java#L189-L200", "https://github.com/networknt/light-4j/blob/2.3.7/ldap-util/src/main/java/com/networknt/ldap/LdapUtil.java#L152-L173", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/networknt-light-4j-2.1.5-before-2.4.0-authentication-bypass-via-empty-ldap-password"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-113682", "GHSA-56rq-859m-p974"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.48, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3647b0a5-2b7a-392c-a2f0-e8266c12bfc8", "product": {"name": "light-4j", "vendor": {"name": "networknt"}}, "product_version": "2.1.5 <2.4.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "13dc36e1-85a5-3755-9061-629917102915", "vendor": {"name": "networknt"}}], "isExploited": false}